## Introduction or Why building functional e-commerce platforms for toddlers can be a thing

‘Toddler’ and ‘e-commerce’ are two words that I didn’t expect to be combining this year, but here we are in this new AI world, and I’m finding that with the latest agents and a little thought on how to harness them, that I'm building plenty of unexpected, but really cool, projects.

The goal of this project was to create a fun toy, while also learning more about e-commerce particularly the Stripe Payments APIs. I wanted an iPad app, with a linked barcode scanner and Stripe card reader. The app would show a checkout screen and there would be toys with QR code stickers. Each could be scanned and then payment made with a special Stripe test credit card.

This was to be my most ambitious agentic side-project yet, for a few reasons:

1. **It involved hardware.** Hardware is fun but historically I've it so time consuming to utilize, with long iteration and debug cycles, that it's just gathered dust. Agents let me cut through that and it was a lot of fun.

